{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1120967-abyssal-intruder-green-sun-s-shadow-the-infectious-nimbus","id":1120967,"title":"Abyssal Intruder: Green Sun's Shadow, the Infectious Nimbus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-26T12:42:24-07:00","id":1120967,"title":"Abyssal Intruder: Green Sun's Shadow, the Infectious Nimbus","content":"Just a homebrew Abyssal manifestation that me and my ST came up with while considering how the Abyss might corrupt one's Nimbus.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Green Sun's Shadow, the Infectious Nimbus</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> The earliest speculated appearance of Green Sun\u2019s Shadow is from 13<sup>th</sup> century India. Awakened records from that time mention a cult by the name of the Viridian Dawn, led by an Awakened whose Shadow Name has been lost to history, and their supposed behind-the-scenes work during the Slave Dynasty. The cult vanishes near the end of the century with no explanation as to why or how, but descriptions of the symptoms of the cult and its possible leader are similar to those inflicted by the Manifestation, earning it its name.<br /> <br /> Green Sun\u2019s Shadow is an infection of the Mage\u2019s Nimbus. Its telltale sign is a greenish corona around a Mage\u2019s traditional Nimbus. Sleepers and Sleepwalkers can contract it, showing in their auras instead, but only among Mages does it become dangerous. Green Sun\u2019s Shadow is communicable and highly contagious, capable of spreading from Nimbus to Nimbus as Mages perform feats of magic. Dense Consilia are especially vulnerable, and due to its nature it can be nearly-impossible to fully scrub from a population once it has taken hold. It is a favored Manifestation of some Scelesti, particularly Nasnasi. It is also an ideological enemy of the Guardians, and in the past they have taken aggressive measures to contain it, holding a story of a city that became so ravaged by its deleterious effects to Wisdom, Willpower, and the use of magic itself that it was expelled from the world and into the Abyss.<br /> <br /> A Mage infected by Green Sun\u2019s Shadow has their Nimbus altered. When Sleepers or Sleepwalkers are exposed to the effect of the Mage\u2019s Nimbus Tilt, the effect does not wear off, instead becoming a persistent Condition. A Sleeper affected by this no longer suffers from the Quiescence Curse at the end of a scene, but becomes afflicted by a compulsion to seek out magic or the Mage whose Nimbus they viewed. There are two ways for a Sleeper to resolve this Condition: to either spend one Willpower Point and endure a Breaking Point as Quiescence asserts itself, or to witness Supernal magic again, increasing a spell\u2019s chance of Paradox. When resolved the second way, Sleepers do not suffer Breaking Points despite the Quiescence, leading to more than one Mage attempting to use this infection as a tool to make others Awaken or Sleepwalk. There are no known instances of this working, but it\u2019s generally considered by those aware of it to be dangerous beyond measure.<br /> <br /> Sleepwalkers suffer less from the effect. When infected they count as Sleepers for the sake of Paradox risk when witnessing Supernal magic. Like Sleepers they can choose to resolve this Condition by either increasing Paradox risk in a spell or spending one Willpower Point, but do not suffer Breaking Points for doing so.<br /> <br /> For Mages who witness an infected Nimbus, the Tilt resolves normally. Instead, they are now a carrier of the infection, spreading it to any others who witness their own Nimbus. Mages similarly have two ways of resolving this: to spend one Willpower Point and make a Wisdom check as the infection tears at their Gnosis and mind on its way out, or to spend one Willpower DOT and suffer no ill consequences. Purging Green Sun\u2019s Shadow does not protect one from subsequent infections, leading some Mages to consider \u201cresponsibly\u201d containing their own infection until an epidemic has passed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":13241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","user":"Biston","date":". 07-26-2017, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}